    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an `initials` field that returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the OpenAPI code generator produces an `initials` field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes `initials` from the entity:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThe value flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` step, which already maps the `Owner` entity to `OwnerDto`, so it appears in `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` (john/smith \u2192 `J.S.`) and the full suite pass.",
